Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) is a branch of AI that focuses on creating new content, data, or solutions by learning patterns from existing information. Unlike traditional AI, which primarily analyzes or classifies data, GenAI can generate text, images, audio, video, and even code that resemble human-created content. It leverages advanced machine learning models, particularly deep learning and neural networks, to understand complex structures in data and produce outputs that are coherent, creative, and contextually relevant.

GenAI has applications across various industries, including content creation, entertainment, healthcare, design, and software development, making it a transformative technology in today’s digital world. Its ability to automate creative processes and assist humans in problem-solving has positioned it as a key driver of innovation in the era of artificial intelligence.
